    <!-- RSI / 공매도 보조 지표 (iOS indicator.* 대응) -->
    <string name="indicator_rsi_info_accessibility">What is RSI?</string>
    <string name="indicator_rsi_info_analogy_body">Think of it like your heart rate right after a run. Too high (overbought) and it may need to cool off; too low (oversold) and it often bounces back.</string>
    <string name="indicator_rsi_info_analogy_title">In plain terms</string>
    <string name="indicator_rsi_info_overbought_body">Above 70 suggests the price may be overheated (overbought).</string>
    <string name="indicator_rsi_info_oversold_body">Below 30 suggests the price may be oversold — often a fear zone.</string>
    <string name="indicator_rsi_info_read_section">How to read it</string>
    <string name="indicator_rsi_info_scale_caption">Below 30 signals oversold (fear); above 70 signals overbought (overheated). The middle (30–70) is neutral.</string>
    <string name="indicator_rsi_info_scale_section">At a glance</string>
    <string name="indicator_rsi_info_support_body">RSI is a separate, price-based check that helps you see whether the Fear Index reading lines up with the market\'s technical momentum.</string>
    <string name="indicator_rsi_info_support_section">Why it\'s here</string>
    <string name="indicator_rsi_info_support_title">A second opinion for the Fear Index</string>
    <string name="indicator_rsi_info_what_body">RSI (Relative Strength Index) measures how fast and how much a price has risen or fallen, on a 0–100 scale.</string>
    <string name="indicator_rsi_info_what_title">What is RSI?</string>
    <string name="indicator_rsi_support_neutral">Price momentum is in neutral territory.</string>
    <string name="indicator_rsi_support_overbought">Price is technically overheated too — leaning toward greed.</string>
    <string name="indicator_rsi_support_oversold">Price is technically oversold too — leaning toward fear.</string>
    <string name="indicator_source_section">Data basis</string>
